# Files that define or can weaken the quality gates (Python).
#
# The gates' only sanctioned escape hatch is editing these files in a reviewed
# PR, so a named human must approve that edit. Enable "Require review from
# Code Owners" in branch protection (../branch-protection.sh does this).
# ADJUST the owner handles per repo: at least two humans with write access.

pyproject.toml         @zaycruz @King-Mayster
uv.lock                @zaycruz @King-Mayster
ruff.toml              @zaycruz @King-Mayster
mypy.ini               @zaycruz @King-Mayster
# Files the tools read BEFORE the ones above: adding one overrides the gate
# config (`.ruff.toml` beats ruff.toml; pytest.ini beats [tool.pytest]; a
# .coveragerc `omit` takes a new module out of diff-coverage). Keep them owned
# even when the repo has none.
.ruff.toml             @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.mypy.ini              @zaycruz @King-Mayster
pytest.ini             @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.pytest.ini            @zaycruz @King-Mayster
tox.ini                @zaycruz @King-Mayster
setup.cfg              @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.coveragerc            @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.jscpd.json            @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.gitleaks.toml         @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.gitleaksignore        @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.gitattributes         @zaycruz @King-Mayster
# Gate docs: the rules agents follow and the repo's gates doc (thresholds, required checks).
AGENTS.md              @zaycruz @King-Mayster
CLAUDE.md              @zaycruz @King-Mayster
docs/engineering/ci-gates.md @zaycruz @King-Mayster
.github/**             @zaycruz @King-Mayster
scripts/ci/**          @zaycruz @King-Mayster
# A conftest.py decides what the tests under it see (it can skip or deselect
# them). Unanchored, so it matches every conftest.py in the repo.
conftest.py            @zaycruz @King-Mayster
# A PR that shrinks a benchmark can hide its own regression (standard §10).
bench/**               @zaycruz @King-Mayster
